A||||3||fierofreek2001||high octane gas stops pinging?||||1||
Z||000000||fierofreek2001||04-23-2001||10:14 AM||||i read a few posts on the forum about higher octane gas possibly stopping that annoying ping* noise that i also have... is an 85 4 cyl coupe going to notice a difference from high octane as opposed to the normal 87 octane?<BR>thanks<BR>steve<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||04-23-2001||10:20 AM||||Knock and ping are caused by predetonation of fuel in the combustion chamber.  The chamber is so hot, that the fuel explodes before the spark plug fires.  This can cause a lot of damage to your engine.<P>Running a higher octane fuel will not cause your engine combustion chambers to run so hot.  If it is cooler, then you wont have predetonation.<P>So yes, you will notice a difference if you run higher octane fuel; your engine wont ping.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Fiero87311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto near completion!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierofreek2001||04-23-2001||10:26 AM||||thanks fierojoe, ill have to give it a try now! <BR>steve||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||04-23-2001||11:49 AM||||The predetonation can be caused by timing set incorrectly or the carbon build up in the cylinder.  ||||reg||1
